In article <HAIRSTON.90Jun15142122@henry.ece.cmu.edu>, hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:
> the oracle is one of those features new in 3.0 that i liked. i now
> find myself thinking that i'd like the oracle better if some things
> were different. i'll get to that, perhaps, at a later time. i'd like
> to know if anyone else has thoughts about the oracle?

By reading this group a lot, the oracles lose their usefulness.  Why
pay for a hint when you've already read it here?  I realize the
oracles are useful for people who don't read this group, so I think
most changes should be additions to current features.

I seem to remember from mythology (and I may be wrong here) that the
oracle's temple was a place of peace.  Creatures in the oracle's
temple would not attack each other, and those that did would suffer
dire consequences.  This would be an interesting feature to add to
nethack oracles.

The usefulness would be limited, however, because there is only one
oracle level in the dungeon, usually in a low level.  Perhaps some
``branch'' temples could be added--these would be similar to the
current oracle rooms, but instead of an oracle there would be a statue
to Athena (do I have the right goddess?).  Only minor consultations
would be available, but the ``no attack'' rule would still apply.
Maybe one of these rooms every five levels or so.

A couple other features:  Some sort of penalty for destroying the 3
statues in the oracle's room (loss of luck or worse).  Of course, if
the idea of branch rooms is used, the penalty for destroying the
statue of the oracle would be quite severe.

The fountain in the oracle's room could also be used for something
besides an ordinary fountain.  Perhaps by paying the oracle, #dipping
in the fountain would have some added benefits (beyond the usual).  Or
drinking from it might give you a vision of some sorts.

